<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/twemoji@latest/dist/twemoji.min.js" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
  <script>
    window.onload = function () {
      twemoji.parse(document.body);
    }
  </script>
</head>

<%# FUIME-DIVERGENCE: this letterhead was Hack Club's, on a document Fuime
    users download.

    It carried the HCB logo from assets.hackclub.com, the heading "The Hack
    Foundation", and that entity's real street address — so every financial
    statement a Fuime venture exported was a document issued in another
    organisation's name, from an address that is not Fuime's. That is a
    trademark problem (CLAUDE.md Rule 7 covers the code, not the brand) and a
    misrepresentation problem, and it is worse here than in a page because a
    statement is the artefact people forward to a parent, a school or an
    accountant.

    ⚠️ NO STREET ADDRESS. Fuime's registered address is not in this codebase
    (LAUNCH_SPEC §1.2 — entity formation), and inventing one on a financial
    statement would be a worse defect than omitting it. Add it here once the
    entity exists; the support address stands in until then. %>
<div>
  <%# wicked_pdf_asset_base64, matching every other PDF template here. A plain
      image_tag renders a broken image under wkhtmltopdf, which cannot resolve
      the asset path — and a broken logo on a financial statement is its own
      kind of unprofessional. %>
  <%= image_tag(wicked_pdf_asset_base64("fuime-logo.png"), height: 60) %>
  <div>
    <h1 style="margin-block: 0">
      Fuime LLC
    </h1>
    <h4 style="margin-block: 0">
      support@fuime.com
    </h4>
  </div>
  <div>
    <u>FINANCIAL STATEMENT</u>
    <span style="text-transform: uppercase">FOR: <b><%= @event.name %></b></span>
    <span>
      <b><%= @start.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></b> to <b><%= @end.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></b>
    </span>
  </div>
</div>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Settled</th>
    <th>Description</th>
    <th style="text-align: center;">ID</th>
    <th style="text-align: center;">Amount</th>
    <th style="text-align: center;">Balance</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><%= @start.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></td>
    <td>PREVIOUS BALANCE</td>
    <td style="text-align: center;"></td>
    <td style="text-align: center;"></td>
    <td style="text-align: center;">
      <%= number_to_currency @start_balance  %>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <% @transactions.reverse.each do |ct| %>
    <% unless ct.likely_account_verification_related? && !organizer_signed_in? %>
      <tr>
        <td style="white-space: nowrap;"><%= ct.date %></td>
        <td><%= transaction_memo(ct) %></td>
        <td style="white-space: nowrap;"><%= ct.local_hcb_code.public_id %></td>
        <td style="text-align: center; white-space: nowrap;"><%= number_to_currency ct.amount %></td>
        <td style="text-align: center; white-space: nowrap;"><%= number_to_currency ct.running_balance %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <tr>
    <td></td>
    <td><i>WITHDRAWN: <%= number_to_currency @withdrawn %>. DEPOSITED: <%= number_to_currency @deposited %>.</i></td>
    <td style="text-align: center;"></td>
    <td style="text-align: center;"></td>
    <td style="text-align: center;">
      <%= number_to_currency @end_balance %>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<%# FUIME-DIVERGENCE: this footer asserted a fiscal-sponsorship relationship
    that does not exist, on a document a family may hand to an accountant.

    It named another organisation's EIN and described the venture's money as a
    "restricted fund provided by The Hack Foundation" — HCB's actual structure,
    and the reason HCB may hold the money at all. Fuime's structure is the
    opposite: under merchant-of-record Fuime LLC is the SELLER, the money is
    Fuime's own revenue from its own sale, and what the operator holds is a
    payable (MOR_MIGRATION_PLAN §1). Restating HCB's sentence here would tell a
    tax preparer something false about where a teenager's money came from.

    L5 also binds this line: no "deposits", no "funds held", nothing implying a
    bank. It says what the document is and stops. %>
<p>
  <i><%= @event.name %></i> sells through Fuime. Fuime LLC is the seller of
  record on those sales and settles the venture&apos;s share to it; this statement
  lists that activity for the period shown.
</p>

<p>
  <i>
    Fuime is a financial technology company, not a bank. Fuime does not hold
    deposits.
  </i>
</p>

<style>
  body {
    padding: 16px;
    color: black;
  }
  h4 {
    font-weight: 400
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 36px;
    border-spacing: 0;
  }
  th {
    background: #ec3750;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-align: left;
    padding-left: 8px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  }
  tr:nth-child(odd) {
      background-color: #ececec;
  }
  td {
    border: none;
  }
  img.emoji {
    height: 1em;
    width: 1em;
    margin: 0 .05em 0 .1em;
    vertical-align: -0.1em;
  }
</style>
